# Running tests (searchconsole-mcp)

## Default: unit tests (always)

From repo root:

```bash
npm test
```

Runs TypeScript checks and **node:test** suites in `test/*.test.ts`. Default tests use a **mocked GSC client** — no live Google calls.

## Mocking GSC

- Inject mocks with `setGscClientForTests` / `resetGscClientForTests` from `src/clients.ts`.
- Call `resetGscClientForTests()` in `beforeEach` when tests override the client.
- See `test/gsc-tools.test.ts` and `test/clients.test.ts` for patterns.
- Do **not** hit the Search Console API in default `npm test`.

## Integration tests (optional, local only)

Only when the user wants live API verification and ADC is configured:

```bash
GSC_INTEGRATION=1 GSC_SITE_URL='https://example.com/' npm run test:integration
```

CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs **`npm test` only** — never require integration for merge.

## When to run

| Change | Command |
|--------|---------|
| `src/`, `test/`, schemas, tools | `npm test` |
| Release / publish prep | `npm test` then `npm run build:prod` |
| Live GSC behavior (user request) | `npm run test:integration` |

## Adding tests

- Add `test/*.test.ts` mirroring the behavior under test.
- Extend existing `describe` blocks and mocks before adding integration coverage.
- Do not add new test frameworks; use built-in **node:test** and **assert/strict**.
- Report pass/fail with evidence. Do not claim tests passed if you did not run them.
